figdown 0.1 bitfield
# `DESCRIPTION-KEY-SPELLING`: the option key `note=` became `description=` (IEEE
# 1685-2022's spelling; SystemRDL's `desc` is barred by RULE 4.2 as an
# abbreviation). The spelling left the LANGUAGE, so the diagnostic fires
# wherever it appears — the `w=`/`h=`/`unit=` placement test (RULE 6.2).
# The reason is the collision ahead: `ANNOTATION-LOCATOR-SPLIT` files `note` as the highest-demand
# v0.2 annotation construct, and that one will be a DRAWN callout.
bitfield hdr "Header" word=32 numbering=msb0
field "A" 16 note="the retired spelling"
field "B" 16 description="the live spelling"
